 "_about": "Apollo 13: the oxygen tank failure on the way to the Moon, the loop around the far side and the return. Event times (GMT, from launch + GET) and the splashdown point are from NASA SP-4029; burns are ignition times. Fra Mauro is the PLANNED landing site (never reached; Apollo 14 later landed there). The trajectory is ILLUSTRATED (72.0 deg flight azimuth, ~100 nmi parking orbit, a ~250 km pass behind the Moon timed by the loss and return of signal); not flight data. 'stack' is Odyssey (CSM) docked with Aquarius (LM). The coast's pace is calibrated so the craft is about 322,000 km from Earth at the explosion (NASA: about 200,000 miles).",
